# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 permu.cc ascsort (under median, quartile1, quartile3, quantile and quartiles in misc.cc, list and matrix forms) took evalf of each element and wrote 0 for every one whose evalf is not a _DOUBLE_; above 14 digits a float element is MPFR (_REAL), so a float list sorted as zeros: at Digits 20 quartile1(evalf([1,2,3,4,5,6])) = 0.0 (2.0 at Digits 12), median(evalf([3,1,2])) = 0.0, quantile(evalf([1,2,3,4,5,6]),0.5) = 0.0, quartiles(evalf([1.5,-2,7,3.25,0.5,4])) = [[0.0],...], median(evalf([[1,5],[3,2],[2,8]])) = [0.0,0.0]; a typed decimal beside integers sorted as 0 too (quartiles([1.5,-2,7,3.25,0.5,4]) at Digits 20 = [[-2.0],[0.0],[0.0],[4.0],[7.0]]). Now a row that holds a real float that is no double (an MPFR value, a _FLOAT_) is sorted by value (MPFR compared exactly with mpfr_cmp and mpfr_cmp_d, stable for equal values) and each element is written back as it is, so an MPFR element keeps its digits; an element with no real float value (a complex, a NaN) is a double 0 as before. A row of doubles and exact numbers keeps the stock double sort.
